<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Identifying Inequality Solutions on a Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00529</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Identifying Inequality Solutions on a Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>684507ee-ef7f-4b1e-a5a8-57d21f002389</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00001">Which graph correctly shows the solution to the inequality <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mstyle><m:mo>≥</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>? Show or explain your reasoning.</para>

          <para id="para-00002">A</para>
          
            <media alt="A number line is shown. There is an open circle on 3. The number line to the right of 3 is highlighted.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_14_01.svg"/>
            </media>
          


          <para id="para-00003">B</para>
          
            <media alt="A number line is shown. There is an open circle on 3. The number line to the left of 3 is highlighted.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_14_02.svg"/>
            </media>
          


          <para id="para-00004">C</para>
          
            <media alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on 3. The number line to the right of 3 is highlighted.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_14_03.svg"/>
            </media>
          


          <para id="para-00005">D</para>
          
            <media alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on 3. The number line to the left of 3 is highlighted.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_14_04.svg"/>
            </media>
          
        </problem>
        
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00006">Compare your answer: Your answers may vary, but here are some samples. Graph C.</para>
          <list id="list-00001">
            <item>I tested 2, 3, and 4 for the values of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, and 3 and 4 make the inequality
              true.</item>
            <item>I solved a related equation and then tested a couple of values on either side of
              the solution.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
